{"type":"Film","id":"DE2017_061","slug":"de2017-061-mein-wunderbares-west-berlin","title":{"native":"Mein wunderbares West-Berlin","english":"My Wonderful West Berlin"},"release":{"type":"Theatrical release","date":"2017-06-29","year":2017},"filmType":"Documentary","directors":[{"id":"Jochen Hick","slug":"jochen-hick","name":"Jochen Hick","birthYear":1960,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"Germany","awards":[]}],"genre":["Documentary – Participatory mode"],"media":{"posterUrl":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt6445290/mediaviewer/rm1605645824/?ref_=tt_ov_i","trailerUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UImkfmaemMY&ab_channel=ThreeDollarBillCinema"},"synopsis":{"native":"Berlin gilt heutzutage als eine der angesagtesten Städte der Welt, was durchaus auch mit der Geschichte der ehemals geteilten Stadt zusammenhängt. Großen Anteil an dem heutigen subkulturellen Lebensgefühl in der deutschen Bundeshauptstadt hatte – wie Regisseur Jochen Hick in „Mein wunderbares West-Berlin“ zeigt – auch die schwule Szene im ehemaligen West-Berlin, die die Partykultur, die sexuelle Vielfalt und die kulturellen Einrichtungen und Institutionen entscheidend prägte – obwohl Schwule in West-Berlin vor allem vor 1969 durch den Paragraph 175 des deutschen Strafgesetzbuches diskriminiert wurden. Um ein Bild vom schwulen Leben im Westteil der Stadt zu zeichnen, lässt Hick politische Aktivisten, Partygänger, Lebenskünstler, Clubbetreiber, Musiker, einen Modemacher, einen DJ und einen Visagisten zu Wort kommen und zeigt teilweise unveröffentlichtes Archivmaterial.","english":"Mathieu is a young and talented black box analyst on a mission to solve the reason behind the deadly crash of a brand new aircraft. Yet, when the case is closed by authorities, Mathieu cannot help but sense there is something wrong with the evidence. As he listens to the tracks again, he starts detecting some seriously disturbing details. Could the tape have been modified? Going against his boss’ orders, Mathieu begins his own rogue investigation – an obsessional and dangerous quest for truth that will quickly threaten far more than his career..."},"production":[{"country":"Germany","share":"Majority coproducer"}],"characters":[],"roles":[{"person":{"id":"Bob Schneider","slug":"bob-schneider","name":"Bob Schneider","birthYear":1962,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"Germany","awards":[]},"role":"Documentary subject"},{"person":{"id":"Egmont Fassbinder","slug":"egmont-fassbinder","name":"Egmont Fassbinder","birthYear":1945,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"Germany","awards":[]},"role":"Documentary subject"},{"person":{"id":"Gerhard Hoffmann","slug":"gerhard-hoffmann","name":"Gerhard Hoffmann","birthYear":1946,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"Germany","awards":[]},"role":"Documentary subject"},{"person":{"id":"Jochen Hick","slug":"jochen-hick","name":"Jochen Hick","birthYear":1960,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"Germany","awards":[]},"role":"Director of the film"},{"person":{"id":"Klaus Schumann","slug":"klaus-schumann","name":"Klaus Schumann","birthYear":1937,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"Germany","awards":[]},"role":"Documentary subject"},{"person":{"id":"Mabel Aschenneller","slug":"mabel-aschenneller","name":"Mabel Aschenneller","birthYear":1951,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"Germany","awards":[]},"role":"Documentary subject"},{"person":{"id":"Peter Hedenström","slug":"peter-hedenstrom","name":"Peter Hedenström","birthYear":1948,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"Germany","awards":[]},"role":"Documentary subject"},{"person":{"id":"René Koch","slug":"rene-koch","name":"René Koch","birthYear":1945,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"Germany","awards":[]},"role":"Documentary subject"},{"person":{"id":"Rolf Eden","slug":"rolf-eden","name":"Rolf Eden","birthYear":1930,"deathYear":2022,"